{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"title":"Custom Dimensions and Units","role":"article"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"text":" ships with a comprehensive set of base dimensions (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/length","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and friends) and derived dimensions (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/speed","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/energy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and more). These cover physics and everyday measurement, but your app almost certainly measures things that aren’t in the SI system too: money, hit points, ingredients, resource points, users, and so on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The good news: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is an open system. Because a dimension is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"just a dictionary of exponent powers","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", you can describe any dimension you can imagine at runtime.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Define a Custom Dimension","anchor":"Define-a-Custom-Dimension","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Create a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" with a dictionary of exponent identifiers. Each key is a dimension name and each value is its power:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Math","","\/\/ A dimension for money, with a single base exponent.","let usdDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"USD\": 1])","","\/\/ A dimension for \"users\", used later in per-user metrics.","let userDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"user\": 1])"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can build compound custom dimensions with the same arithmetic used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internally: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"text":" multiplies dimensions, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"text":" divides them, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*"},{"text":" with an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" raises a dimension to a power:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let revenuePerUser = usdDimension - userDimension   \/\/ [\"USD\": 1, \"user\": -1]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Define Custom Units","anchor":"Define-Custom-Units","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom dimensions don’t have a compile-time type, so use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" as the type-level parameter and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/NamedUnit","type":"reference"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"create units. Pass a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/LinearConverter","isActive":true},{"text":" (for a simple scale) or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/OffsetConverter","type":"reference"},{"text":" (for a scale plus an offset) to handle conversions:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let usdUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"$\",","    dimension: usdDimension,","    converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.0)",")","","\/\/ EUR is defined relative to the same base dimension.","let eurUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"€\",","    dimension: usdDimension,","    converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.09)",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keep the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"PhysicalDimension","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value (here ","type":"text"},{"code":"usdDimension","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") for every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unit in a family. The framework only converts between units whose dimensions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match, so sharing the exact same value makes your money interchangeable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Tip","type":"aside"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Convert-Between-Custom-Units","text":"Convert Between Custom Units"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom units convert exactly like the built-in ones:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let walletInEur = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: eurUnit)","let walletInUsd = walletInEur.converted(to: usdUnit)","","print(walletInUsd.value) \/\/ 109.0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Combine Custom Units with Built-In Ones","anchor":"Combine-Custom-Units-with-Built-In-Ones","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom dimensions participate in dimensional arithmetic too. Here a currency","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dimension combines with the built-in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" dimension:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let hourlyRate = Quantity(value: 50.0, unit: usdUnit) \/ Quantity(value: 1.0, unit: Units.hour)","","print(hourlyRate.value)          \/\/ 50.0","print(hourlyRate.unit.dimension) \/\/ [\"USD\": 1, \"time\": -1]","print(hourlyRate.unit.symbol)    \/\/ \"($\/h)\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Use the Currency Dimension","anchor":"Use-the-Currency-Dimension","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If your custom dimension happens to be currency, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"text":" already defines a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/currency","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" dimension and a built-in library of world","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"currencies (and cryptocurrencies) in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Currency units automatically","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"place their symbol before the value when formatting:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let gift = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: Units.usd)","print(gift.formatted()) \/\/ \"$100.00\"","","\/\/ Resolve units from ISO 4217 codes at runtime.","if let currency = Units.currency(for: \"SEK\") {","    print(currency.symbol) \/\/ \"kr\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"What’s Next?","anchor":"Whats-Next","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to lock custom units into a compile-time dimension in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explore "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"type":"text","text":" to see the breadth of units provided out of the box."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/customdimensions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Extend ","type":"text"},{"code":"Math","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with your own physical dimensions and units—currency, points, gameplay metrics, or anything else your app measures.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Extending-the-Framework","generated":true,"title":"Extending the Framework","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"references":{"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type representing a physical dimension as a canonical dictionary of base SI dimension exponents."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PhysicalDimension"}],"title":"PhysicalDimension","url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PhysicalDimension"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension/energy":{"url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension\/energy","type":"topic","title":"energy","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The dimension of energy ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"force × length"},{"type":"text","text":", SI unit: joule)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/energy","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"energy","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": `Self`","kind":"text